# Vendored third-party code must stay byte-identical to what upstream published,
# so that anyone can re-verify it against the published hashes. This repo is
# cloned on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites line endings on
# checkout — that alone would make leaflet.js hash differently from the file
# unpkg serves, and the whole point of vendoring is being able to prove what
# shipped. -text disables the conversion in both directions.
assets/vendor/** -text
